/board.js** - Board state management, match detection, gravity\n**js/renderer.js** - Canvas rendering\n**js/input.js** - Touch input handling\n**js/animation.js** - Animation system\n**js/score.js** - Score management\n**js/game.js** - Game state machine (start, play, end)\n\nWait, having `game.js` at root and `js/game.js` is confusing. Let me rename.\n\n**game.js** - Entry point\n**js/config.js** - Configuration\n**js/board.js** - Board logic\n**js/renderer.js** - Rendering\n**js/input.js** - Input handling\n**js/animation.js** - Animations\n**js/score-manager.js** - Score system\n**js/game-state.js** - Game state machine\n\nLet me write the code. I'll create all files at once.\n\nActually, I should be practical. For a Douyin mini-game prototype, the code should be:\n1. Complete and runnable\n2. Well-organized\n3. Not overly complex\n4. Visually appealing with canvas drawing\n\nLet me write a complete implementation. I'll make the game work well with:\n- Smooth animations\n- Good visual effects\n- Complete game mechanics\n- Douyin API compatibility\n\nLet me start coding all files. I need to create the directory first, then write all files.\n\nLet me think about the game design:\n\n**Piece Types**: 6 types with distinct colors\n- Red, Blue, Green, Yellow, Purple, Orange\n\n**Board**: 8x8 grid\n\n**Mechanics**:\n- Tap to select a piece (highlight it)\n- Tap an adjacent piece to swap\n- If swap creates a match (3+), remove matches\n- If no match, swap back\n- Gravity pulls pieces down\n- New pieces fill from top\n- Check for cascading matches\n- Chain combos multiply score\n\n**Scoring**:\n- 3 match: 100 points\n- 4 match: 200 points\n- 5 match: 500 points\n- Combo multiplier: x1, x2, x3...\n- Level target scores\n\n**Game Modes**:\n- Moves mode: X moves to reach target score\n- Start with level 1, 30 moves, target 3000\n\n**UI Layout (portrait)**:\n- Top: Score bar (score, level, moves left)\n- Middle: Game board (8x8)\n- Bottom: Reset button\n\nLet me code this now